parsePosix is operation
parsePosix purpose "Read a POSIX TZ string (std offset [dst [offset] [,start[/time],end[/time]]]) into the zone's rule: 1, or 0 for one whose name is missing, which leaves the empty names and a zero offset as glibc does, and a name with no offset after it keeps its offset 0 and, on Linux, an empty daylight name (on Windows, where no file would have named the zone, the standard name); daylight time with no rules follows the United States's (M3.2.0, M11.1.0)"
