makeTimeIn is operation
makeTimeIn purpose "mktime for the zone already loaded: the time of a struct tm in it, which is made to hold the normalized fields with tm_wday, tm_yday, tm_isdst, tm_gmtoff, and tm_zone; the search is glibc's (gnulib's mktime): it guesses from the offset the last call found, converges on the time whose fields match, looks for a nearby time of the requested tm_isdst, and in a spring-forward gap chooses between the two times it oscillates between; -1 with EOVERFLOW when no time fits"
makeTimeIn invariant normalizes "\"Gives the time whose local fields are the struct tm's, and rewrites the struct tm normalized\""
